    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3f8c147f_3e6586e9",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/fingerprint_egis660_pal.c",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 1438457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-20T10:03:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So all this complexity is introduced to workaround the cs pin high problem? Please let me know first next time. I spent some time trying to understand this. We can just fix it in a proper way.\n\nThe `fp_sensor_unlock` is not directly related to CS pin. It blocks access to sensor for other tasks while some multiple SPI transfers is ongoing (`leave_cs_asserted` is true). `spi_release_dt` is used to release the CS pin. You missed one important configuration in the FPS driver, which is `SPI_HOLD_ON_CS`, as in [FPC1025](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/fingerprint_fpc1025.c;l\u003d538). That should cause in leaving the CS pin asserted after the SPI transaction, till `spi_release_dt` is called. The [description](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/include/zephyr/drivers/spi.h#L181) says that is has to be supported by hardware + SPI driver, you can check with Jacob (author of SPI driver in ET171) if that\u0027s the case.",
      "parentUuid": "eb602477_5b54fdf7",
      "revId": "2f0c74bf3165492155d6c471fcef17ec208e8503",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "626962ca_f00ed3c4",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/fingerprint_egis660_pal.c",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 4412439
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-22T03:40:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We also tried to add `SPI_HOLD_ON_CS` in FPS driver, but still can not keep CS high when `leave_cs_asserted` is true, so we adding this workaround for now. But we are working on removing the `leave_cs_asserted` parameter in private library.",
      "parentUuid": "3f8c147f_3e6586e9",
      "revId": "2f0c74bf3165492155d6c471fcef17ec208e8503",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
